README.md:978:**Option 1: Claude Code Skill** (recommended for Claude Code users)
README.md:985:**Option 2: OpenCode** (has built-in Claude skill compatibility)
README.md:1000:**Option 3: Any LLM** (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, etc.)
README.md:1016:<summary><b>How is this different from just using tmux?</b></summary>
README.md:1018:Agent Deck adds AI-specific intelligence on top of tmux: smart status detection (knows when Claude is thinking vs. waiting), session forking with context inheritance, MCP management, global search across conversations, and organized groups. Think of it as tmux plus AI awareness.
README.md:1030:<summary><b>Can I use different Claude accounts/configs per profile?</b></summary>
README.md:1032:Yes. Set a global Claude config dir, then add optional per-profile overrides in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agent-deck/config.toml` (default `~/.config/agent-deck/config.toml`):
README.md:1048:You can verify which Claude config path is active with:
README.md:1060:<summary><b>Will it interfere with my existing tmux setup?</b></summary>
README.md:1062:No. Agent Deck creates its own tmux sessions with the prefix `agentdeck_*`. Your existing sessions are untouched. The installer backs up your `~/.tmux.conf` before adding optional config, and you can skip it with `--skip-tmux-config`.
